#### 8. Exception Handling (testsmells.org — core smell)

**Test:** `ProcessOrder_EmptyOrder_ThrowsValidationError` (line 110)
**Problem:** Manual `try/catch` instead of the framework's `Assert.ThrowsException<T>`.

```csharp
// SMELLY
try
{
    processor.ProcessOrder(order);
    Assert.Fail("Expected an exception but none was thrown");
}
catch (ValidationException ex)
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
}
```

**Note:** This is a capture-and-assert pattern (it does verify the message), so it's functional — but still a smell because `Assert.Fail` is easy to forget and MSTest has a built-in.

**Fix:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void ProcessOrder_EmptyOrder_ThrowsValidationError()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order();

    var ex = Assert.ThrowsException<ValidationException>(
        () => processor.ProcessOrder(order));

    Assert.AreEqual("Order must contain at least one item", ex.Message);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** If `Assert.Fail` is accidentally removed, the test silently passes when no exception is thrown.

